class:: ShaderFFTTexture
summary:: Controlled-rate FFT-magnitude stream for SCShader's spectrum binding
categories:: External>Graphics
related:: Guides/SCShader, Classes/ShaderBuffer, Classes/ShaderWaveformTexture, Classes/Shader

description::
ShaderFFTTexture reads a mono audio bus, computes a standard SuperCollider FFT, extracts linear magnitudes, and maintains them in an owned link::Classes/ShaderBuffer::. Its name describes the shader-facing result: a one-row Float32 GPU texture at the fixed code::spectrum:: binding, not a general image link::Classes/ShaderTexture::. The stream is sent from code::scsynth:: by controlled-rate code::SendReply:: packets, then relayed from the language to the renderer as float32 OSC blobs.

The requested code::rate:: is an upper target rate. Replies are quantized to FFT-window boundaries and reduced with code::PulseDivider::, so an FFT whose hop rate is below the requested rate cannot exceed its natural update rate. Magnitudes are raw linear FFT-bin values; normalize, compress, or log-scale them in the shader or in a future mapping layer. The implementation extracts demand-rate bins in groups of at most 32 because of SuperCollider's Demand input limit.

Relative to vanilla link::Classes/FFT::, this class keeps FFT work in code::scsynth:: but packages the resulting magnitudes for GPU use. It does not make FFT data audio-rate in the renderer and has no phase, mel, chroma, or shared-memory modes.

classmethods::

method:: new

argument:: server
Booted audio Server that owns code::source::.

argument:: source
Non-negative mono audio-bus index.

argument:: fftSize
Power-of-two FFT size from 64 through 16384. Defaults to 2048. The ShaderBuffer has code::fftSize / 2:: bins.

argument:: rate
Positive desired maximum reply rate in Hz. Defaults to 30.

argument:: shaderServer
Ready ShaderServer that owns the resulting ShaderBuffer. Defaults to code::ShaderServer.default::.

instancemethods::

method:: start

discussion::
Creates the analysis Synth and OSC responder. Call it from a Routine because it synchronizes the generated SynthDef. The Synth is placed at the audio server's default-group tail so ordinary sources write their bus first.

method:: free

discussion::
Frees the OSC responder, analysis Synth, and owned ShaderBuffer.

examples::

This example uses the packaged extension. Run one demo at a time and wait for setup to finish. It creates its own resources; no earlier example is required. See link::Guides/SCShader:: for the full walkthrough.

code::
(
var source = ShaderDef.filenameSymbol.asString.dirname.dirname +/+ "shaders/spectrum_bars.wgsl";
v = ShaderServer.new(\guideFFT);
v.waitForBoot { |server|
    d = ShaderDef(\guideSpectrum, source);
    x = Shader(d, [\amount, 0.8], server);
    s.waitForBoot {
        ~scShaderSetup = Routine({
            var deadline = Main.elapsedTime + 5;
            while({ x.isRunning.not and: { Main.elapsedTime < deadline } }, { 0.01.wait });
            if(x.isRunning.not) { Error("Shader did not become ready; inspect x.lastError.").throw };
            ~scShaderSample = Buffer.readChannel(s, ExampleFiles.child, channels: [0]);
            ~scShaderAudioBus = Bus.audio(s, 1);
            SynthDef(\scShaderGuideSource, { |out = 0, bufnum = 0|
                var signal = PlayBuf.ar(1, bufnum, BufRateScale.kr(bufnum), loop: 1);
                // signal = SoundIn.ar(0); // optional live input instead
                signal = signal * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.1);
                Out.ar(out, signal);
                Out.ar(0, (signal * 0.12) ! 2);
            }).add;
            s.sync; // buffer and SynthDef must be ready before playback
            ~scShaderAudio = Synth(\scShaderGuideSource,
                [\out, ~scShaderAudioBus.index, \bufnum, ~scShaderSample.bufnum]);
            ~scShaderFFT = ShaderFFTTexture(s, ~scShaderAudioBus.index, 2048, 30, server);
            ~scShaderFFT.start;
            x.setTexture(\spectrum, ~scShaderFFT);
        }).play(SystemClock);
    };
};
)
::

Cleanup before starting another example; wait for any renderer window to close:

code::
(
~scShaderSetup.tryPerform(\stop);
x.tryPerform(\free);
~scShaderFFT.tryPerform(\free);
~scShaderAudio.tryPerform(\free);
~scShaderAudioBus.tryPerform(\free);
~scShaderSample.tryPerform(\free);
d.tryPerform(\free); v.free;
// Leave the audio server running; do not stop unrelated audio.
)
::

